"Comms button along the bottom edge of your console to the right. Once "
"communications are open, click the Check with docking port authority button "
"to determine the docking protocol. Report the protocol to your crew."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_06_early_evaluation_exercise.lua:10494
msgctxt "msgHelms"
msgid ""
"You might be asked to jump into the nearby nebula so that a freighter can be "
"scanned."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_06_early_evaluation_exercise.lua:10515
#, lua-format
msgctxt "msgScience"
msgid ""
"Start scanning the target at bearing %.1f right away. Report the type of "
"ship as soon as you finish the simple scan. Then start the deep scan. The "
"default keyboard shortcut is S to start the scan. After completing the deep "
"scan, get the scanned ship's strongest shield deflection frequency by "
"hovering over the lowest, reddest point on the bar graph. Report that "
"frequency."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_06_early_evaluation_exercise.lua:10524
msgctxt "msgRelay"
msgid ""
"Send a probe to the middle of the nearest nebula: click the launch probe "
"button, then click the middle of the nebula. Once it's there, link it to "
"science. Be ready to report the ship type and the frequency as soon as "
"Science completes each scan."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_06_early_evaluation_exercise.lua:10532
#, lua-format
msgctxt "msgOperations"
msgid ""
"Start scanning the target at bearing %.1f right away. There are likely more "
"targets in the nebula, so you should request that helm or tactical take you "
"closer to the nebula. Report the type of ship as soon as you finish the "
"simple scan. Then start the deep scan. The default keyboard shortcut is S to "
"start the scan. After completing the deep scan, get the scanned ship's "
"strongest shield deflection frequency by hovering over the lowest, reddest "
"point on the bar graph. Report that frequency. Once you scan the other "
"targets that are likely in the nebula, you will need to exit the nebula to "
"report their characteristics to %s."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_06_early_evaluation_exercise.lua:10547
msgctxt "msgHelms"
msgid ""
"Jump to the enemy freighter if it's farther than 5 units away. Get the "
"bearing and distance from Science or Operations, subtract 2 units to place "
"you in optimal firing range. Once you're near, rotate to point the left or "
"right tube to the enemy. He'll try to run away, so be ready to angle the "
"tube to lead the HVLIs in front of the enemy freighter."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_06_early_evaluation_exercise.lua:10558
msgctxt "msgWeapons"
msgid ""
"Load up HVLIs on both sides. You may have to ask Engineering for power to "
"missile systems."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_06_early_evaluation_exercise.lua:10581
msgctxt "msgEngineer"
msgid ""
"Raise power to missile systems to 100%. Put even more in along with coolant "
"to make them load faster. Be ready to add power to impulse and/or "
"maneuvering as requested."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_06_early_evaluation_exercise.lua:10600
msgctxt "msgScience"
msgid ""
"Select the enemy freighter. Use radar or probe view as applicable. Provide "
"bearing and distance to freighter to crew. You can find it along the right "
"of your console screen."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_06_early_evaluation_exercise.lua:10611
msgctxt "msgOperations"
msgid ""
"Provide bearing and range to enemy freighter. If nebula obscures your view, "
"estimate based on recent scans, otherwise click the enemy freighter and read "
"the bearing and distance from your console."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_06_early_evaluation_exercise.lua:10622
msgctxt "msgRelay"
msgid ""
"Hack enemy ships once they are in range either via probe or your ship. "
"Impulse engines for the fighter types is a good choice since it makes it "
"easier to shoot them down."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_06_early_evaluation_exercise.lua:10634
msgctxt "msgHelms"
msgid ""
"You will have to go to the distressed freighter to help defend it against "
"Kraylor and to help repair it. You may have to pick up parts from your home "
"station. Deciding which to do first will be up to your commanding officer or "
"CO. Be thinking about both options."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_06_early_evaluation_exercise.lua:10645
msgctxt "msgWeapons"
msgid ""
"Your beams are fully functional. Your missiles have been returned to you. "
"Load up your tubes in preparation for combat. Homing missiles are "
"recommended. Even homing missiles can be dodged by the enemy. Try for as "
"straight a shot as possible."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_06_early_evaluation_exercise.lua:10668
msgctxt "msgEngineer"
msgid ""
"Pay careful attention to what systems are used and give them additional "
"power when needed (along with coolant). Remember the docking/undocking "
"protocol (no missile energy)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_06_early_evaluation_exercise.lua:10687
msgctxt "msgScience"
msgid ""
"Scan the distressed Arlenian freighter as soon as you can (twice). After the "
"second scan, get the impulse engine damage percentage by clicking the "
"Tactical widget and selecting Systems. Report it to Relay who will report it "
"to the home station."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_06_early_evaluation_exercise.lua:10698
msgctxt "msgRelay"
msgid ""
"Launch probes to cover the sector where the distressed Arlenian freighter is "
"located. Link the probe that finds the freighter to science. Contact the "
"freighter. Report Science's scan results to your home station."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_06_early_evaluation_exercise.lua:10709
msgctxt "msgOperations"
msgid ""
"Contact the distressed Arlenian freighter, then scan the freighter as soon "
"as you can (twice). After the second scan, get the impulse engine damage "
"percentage by clicking the Tactical widget and selecting Systems. Report it "
"to the home station."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_06_early_evaluation_exercise.lua:10721
msgctxt "msgHelms"
msgid ""
"Use warp to approach but not intersect the planets and moons in motion. "
"Intersetion will damage and quickly destroy your ship. Use guidance from "
"Relay/Science/Operations for good approach vectors. Warn Engineering when "
"you use warp, especially anything above warp one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_06_early_evaluation_exercise.lua:10732
msgctxt "msgWeapons"
msgid ""
"Watch for enemy targets of opportunity. The planets and moons are far more "
"dangerous, but if you leave the enemies alone, eventually, they will start "
"attacking your home station."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_06_early_evaluation_exercise.lua:10755
msgctxt "msgEngineer"
msgid ""
"Suggested default settings: 50% coolant in warp, 50% coolant in maneuvering, "
"150% power in maneuvering, remaining systems: 100%, remainig coolant: 0. "
"Watch energy carefully and let the commanding officer know when you get "
"below 200 so you can dock and get more. The reactor will help, but charging "
"at a station is more efficient."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_06_early_evaluation_exercise.lua:11601
#, lua-format
msgctxt "human-incCall"
msgid "You completed the research task. Destroy any Kraylor headed for %s"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_06_early_evaluation_exercise.lua:11610
msgctxt "goal-shipLog"
msgid ""
"You completed the research task. Destroy any Kraylor that were headed for "
"your home base"
msgstr ""

